  "version": "0.7.2-beta.1",
  "notes": "## Changes since `v0.7.1`\n\n### UI and usability\n\n- keep the islands frame legible over any desktop with blur on: the title bar and the ground around the cards took only 0.6 of the configured opacity, about 54% at 90%, because the cards lay over the ground and had to stay below the configured opacity together with it; so a light desktop washed out the bar's icons and a dark one swallowed the inactive tabs; the ground now takes the bars' opacity, as the title bar does in the classic style, and is no longer painted behind the cards, which tint the blur directly: the frame is the content area's border, the gaps are the dividers, and a card's rounded corners are filled by its own shadow cut to its box ([ee216f88](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/commit/ee216f88b0fa5cf5f9e02e33d120aa461474f6cf))\n\n**Full comparison:** [v0.7.1...v0.7.2-beta.1](https://github.com/330079598/tTerm/compare/v0.7.1...v0.7.2-beta.1)",
